+# Affidavit and August 24 update: partial controls for the disputed FISA drafting
+
+**The court's August 17 affidavit adds a contemporaneous statement to the drafting comparison. The August 24 update adds an earlier written account of the search-route disagreement.** Neither establishes the identity of the missing August 28 draft attachments, the accuracy of all interview summaries, a formal legal decision or the outcome of a proposed search. This is an additive follow-up to the [349/693 comparison](../moussaoui-349-693-comparison-2026-10-29/README.md); its earlier source records and report remain unchanged.
+
+## 32: a sworn statement, with a narrower join than the index title alone supplies
+
+The [official court index](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense.html) links exhibit **32** to **[032.pdf](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/032.pdf)**. The preceding study's ready-next TODO used the unpadded URL32.pdf. This record preserves and corrects that locator; it is an error in our research pointer, not evidence of historical alteration or current suppression. The actual court-linked PDF was retrieved successfully and both pages were read.
+
+Physical page **1** identifies a sworn witness statement in INS affidavit form, executed at Bloomington on **08/17/2001**, in English, with no interpreter indicated. It reports statements attributed to the person the witness knew as Shaqil. This is an official court-hosted scan of an apparent contemporary statement, not native authentication of handwriting, signatures, voluntariness or the complete surrounding interview.
+
+The useful comparisons are different in strength:
+
+| Actual affidavit location | Held LHM or drafting record | What the comparison establishes and leaves open |
+|---|---|---|
+| **32 p1, numbered item1** describes conditional secret harm against a nonbeliever harming a Muslim and identifies Jews and Christians in that reported category. | **693 p4 third bullet;347 p7/LHM4 third bullet** explicitly attribute a corresponding claim to a sworn statement signed08/17. | A specific date/content correspondence to the LHM's **third bullet**, not authenticated proof that this exact copy was the source received by the drafter. The claims are the witness's attributed statements, not independently verified beliefs or acts. |
+| **32 p1, item3** attributes a generalized assertion that a true Muslim should train himself to fight by building his body and being ready. | **349 p1 item2** objects to replacing preparing himself to fight with train together in defensive tactics. **693 p4 first bullet and347 p7 first bullet** attribute preparing to fight to an **08/16 interview**. | The held affidavit contains fight-training language and does not display together/defensive-tactics wording in its five items. But its generalized formulation, date and referent are not identical to the August16 interview attribution. It cannot alone establish which proposed paraphrase accurately represents that separate interview. |
+| **32 p1–2, all five numbered items** concern attributed beliefs, conflict discussion, training, a sheikh and countries; the document does not display the disputed hearing-plan, aviation-payment, employment or joyride question-and-answer passages. | **349 p1 items3–5;350 p1 items3–5;693 p4 bullets2,4,5;347 p7 corresponding bullets**. | This affidavit does not supply the missing statement inputs for those disputes. The absence is limited to these two pages; it is not evidence no such answers were given elsewhere or that material was removed. |
+
+The affidavit therefore advances **DRAFT-T02** only partially. It neither resolves Jones's objection nor independently validates Maltbie's accuracy assertion. Nor does it establish agreement to a particular attack, a specific operational plan or a government actor's involvement. The August16 original interview/questions, later questioning, exact drafts and their custody/version joins remain the discriminating inputs.
+
+## 348: earlier written disagreement, and an explicitly conditional alternative
+
+[Exhibit348](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/348.pdf), physical page **1**, is displayed as a Samit message to Jones, Weiss and Humble, subject **Update**, dated **8/24/01 10:31AM**; no timezone is supplied. All of this one-page copy was read. It contains no native thread/transport headers or draft attachment.
+
+In the **second body paragraph**, Samit says it **seems** that ITOS/RFU has thus far determined there is neither reasonable suspicion of a federal felony in progress nor a foreign-power connection for the respective criminal/FISA routes. He explicitly disagrees while acknowledging HQ's authority. These are **Samit's attributed account and legal-threshold wording**, not this review's statement of governing law, an acquired HQ opinion, an attorney's own assessment or a judicial ruling. The word seems and the provisional thus-far framing remain material.
+
+The **three middle bullets** describe a feared, conditional option: deportation to the **UK**, with property including747 manuals unsearched; potential pickup at Heathrow depends on the British authorities' legal tools; Samit worries about a preceding **8hours** in which computer data or paperwork could become unavailable. This is a predicted opportunity/risk, not an established deletion, actual deportation itinerary, authorized search, act of sabotage or evidence that eight hours actually elapsed. Handwritten British authorities annotations sit beside redacted blocks; they do not identify the exact concealed agency, author or original wording. No redaction is reconstructed.
+
+The **closing request** seeks British information supporting either a foreign-power connection or a federal offense. It attributes to RFU the apparent requirement for a named group or country. That wording is a participant's description of the review obstacle. It remains beside the later HQ participant account in [351](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/351.pdf), not a replacement for the underlying legal-unit advice. The latter was examined in the [preceding drafting study](../moussaoui-fisa-draft-exchanges-2026-10-29/README.md); it was not newly reread in this unit.
+
+## Preserve the different routes and dates
+
+The new348 message can be compared with the previously acquired [347 urgent request](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/347.pdf), the later [334 both-route/France account](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/334.pdf) and [701 criminal-warrant trail](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/defense/701.pdf), without treating any one as the final disposition. The new record is an **August24** account of disagreement and a conditional **UK** alternative. The **September10** record discusses a **France** alternative, while701 documents efforts involving criminal warrants. The timing, proposed destinations, requested acts and source authorship remain separate. They are not silently harmonized, treated as simultaneous contradictory completed events or converted into an established order to permit an attack.
+
+The reported disagreement is now documented earlier in the held contemporaneous record. It is **not independent corroboration of HQ's actual decision**, because348 and334 repeat the same participant's account. The available material contains genuine warning and disagreement as well as efforts to obtain additional information and search authority. Those efforts matter when testing a hypothesis of deliberate suppression, but do not by themselves decide the intent or adequacy of the response. Actual legal advice, evidentiary package, referral/nonreferral, instructions and executed outcomes remain needed.
+
+No May2003 corrected FAA response, delivery acknowledgment, signed administrative action/no-action decision, OIG recommendation implementation/closure or controlling case-specific policy record was acquired here. The five-track work plan's original18 requirements remain open. Nor does this study connect Moussaoui's search decisions to a Saudi, UMS/Israeli or Cheney/Halliburton operation; each proposed actor/mechanism requires its own source-supported link.
+
+## Reading, preservation and test boundaries
+
+- **New source reading:** all **three pages** of32/348 visually read at145dpi. The PDFs have no extractable text on any page and no passively exposed attachment names. These observations describe the court copies, not the existence of original attachments or interviews.
+- **Prior source reinspection:**349 p1,350 p1,693 p4 and347 p7, **four pages**. Other references rely on the previously preserved studies and are not claimed as fresh full-document readings.
+- **Method:** exact source-byte hashes and page counts, passive text/attachment enumeration, local page renders and selected-clause comparison. No OCR, forensic signature/handwriting authentication, native email reconstruction, whole-document character diff or legal/causal adjudication was performed.
+- **Source independence:** the INS statement and FBI summaries have a potential common underlying witness; repetition is not a second independent witness. Samit's two messages are not two independent decision makers confirming HQ's rationale.
+- **Public payload:** original research notes, URLs, hashes, reading/checklist/TODO records and exact additive text diff. Raw scans, signatures, private correspondence, contact/identity numbers and reconstructed redacted identities are excluded. Source bytes remain unchanged in the native research store.
+
+[SOURCES.json](SOURCES.json) gives acquisition/hash/reading scopes. [CLAUSE-COMPARISON.json](CLAUSE-COMPARISON.json) preserves the limited joins. [OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) carries forward **DRAFT-T01–T06** and next genuinely untried routes. [REVIEW-AND-CHECKS.json](REVIEW-AND-CHECKS.json) separates the request checklist from preservation checks. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) is the exact addition against absence at the new public paths; earlier findings are unchanged, not rewritten.
